- op: discuss  # f984
  at: '2026-06-02T03:52:24Z'  # f984
  by: agent  # f984
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f984
  clock: 3  # f984
  nonce: f984  # f984
  message: "Pass-22 investigation correction.\n\nThe original framing claimed display_label on Class C (unresolved external) violated ADR-0033's stated invariant. Re-reading spec_validator.py:762-789 shows the validator EXPLICITLY exempts kind='external_symbol' and kind='file' from the display_label check, citing ir.py:1285 where external-symbol Class C nodes are synthesized with display_label as their canonical printable form: 'this is the ADR-0032 typed-sibling pattern applied to externals, not a Class A leak'.\n\nSo Class C carrying display_label is INTENDED, not a violation. The validator (axis_conformance + cross_field) is correctly designed for the three-class model: A=real-source (no display_label), B=protocol-synth (display_label expected), C=external-symbol/file (display_label expected as boundary identity).\n\nThe REAL residual: Class B (262 protocol-synth nodes per ADR-0031) all have display_label=None. ADR-0032 reserves display_label for synthetic stand-ins; Class B is the canonical synthetic-stand-in case. The validator's cross_field check only enforces the contrapositive ('no display_label on Class A') and does NOT check the affirmative ('Class B should have display_label populated'). Producers (linkers that emit Class B nodes) currently do not populate display_label.\n\nCorrected scope:\n- This is a producer-side gap (linkers don't populate display_label on Class B) AND a validator-class-scope gap (only one direction of the invariant is enforced).\n- Downgrade P0 -> P2: real but not an emergency; the data is consistent within each class, just incomplete on Class B.\n- The 'validator class scope only enforces contrapositive' pattern is META-level: every cross_field invariant in spec_validator.py could have the same one-sided check. Worth keeping as a META."  # f984
- op: discuss  # d7ac
