  message: "Satisfied — synthetic:F2 (5a), PR #226 (merged dev c058b59a55). Both halves of the display_label biconditional now hold for Class-B. PRODUCER: populate_synthetic_class_b_identity (analyze/base.py, post-linker) stamps display_label on Class-B protocol-synth nodes (language=None + protocol_origin) that linkers left null. VALIDATOR: the spec_validator Class-B canary gained the affirmative 'Class-B SHOULD carry display_label' check (it previously checked stable_id/fingerprint/discovery_language/origin but not display_label; the Class-A contrapositive already forbade it on real source). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (live repro on merged dev via production code): a Class-B Symbol with display_label=None -> validate_ir flags Symbol.display_label (flagged-when-missing=True); populate_synthetic_class_b_identity fills it (None -> 'ipc:req:chan'); re-validate -> not flagged (flagged-after-fill=False). Production-path tests: test_class_b_missing_display_label_is_flagged / _with_display_label_not_flagged (validator) + the TestPopulateSyntheticClassBIdentity class (producer). The statement's first clause (Class-C external_symbol carrying display_label) is the pass-22 correction = INTENDED (validator exempts kind in {file, external_symbol}); the real residual was the Class-B omission + the two-class-blind validator, both now closed."  # 18c2
